# Maintenance-state fixture: what a store looks like AFTER a few months of use.
# Same JSONL shape as memories.jsonl, plus the state the graded dataset never
# carries: age_days (backdates created_at, so decay is observable), resolved
# (a resolve verdict), project ("_global" for a shared row searched from the
# project), and supersedes (keys this memory REPLACES, so demotion has real
# edges — the newer memory lists the older one). `importance` is NOT correlated
# with role: a stale copy is sometimes the most important-looking memory in the
# store, which is the point. A resolved row's category is one SetResolved will
# actually stamp — convention and preference are exempt, so a store cannot hold
# a resolved convention.
# maintenance_queries.jsonl grades against this file; maintenance_embeddings.json
# holds the vectors, regenerated via Ollama POST /api/embed (nomic-embed-text:v1.5,
# 768 dims) when this file changes. See docs/benchmarks.md ("Maintenance state").
